  "description": "Proactive pruning works for statutory nuisance abatement.\r - Norway maple - Deadwood \u00135cm. Remove single dead limb from southern canopy.  At 5m. \r - Rowan - Crown Reduction. Crown reduced by 4-5m focus on western extent and leave weight in the easten canopy.  Retain inner canopy growth. Prune back to suitable sublateral growth. \r - Himalayan birch 'Jacquemontii'- Crown Lift. Crown lift low canopy over footpath to 2.5m.  Prune back to suitable sublateral growth. \r - Himalayan birch 'Jacquemontii'. Crown Reduction. Reduce southern canopy by 2-3m where possible.  This is to alleviate loading of poor included union.  Prune to suitable sublateral growth.  Also remove major deadwood.\r - Sycamore\t Sever Ivy. Sever and remove ivy from 0-100cm above ground level.",
